2026-10-11T05:31:54.4238419Z [1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer[0m
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4314705Z [32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4323010Z [0m
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4323299Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4323609Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4323785Z 
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4324328Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4324853Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4325082Z 
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4325298Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4325680Z    if you are ready to continue.
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4325872Z 
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4326459Z 3. Create the system users [34m(uids [30001..30008])[0m and groups [34m(gid 30000)[0m
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4326925Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4327290Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4327578Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4327715Z 
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4327906Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4328106Z 
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4328321Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4328621Z    can use Nix.
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4328724Z 
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4328828Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4328954Z 
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4329260Z [32m[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4329876Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4333169Z 
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4333252Z I will:
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4333346Z 
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4333529Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4333877Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4334242Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4334597Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4334821Z  - install Nix in /nix
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4335053Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4335507Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4335709Z    /root
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4562913Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4563374Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4577258Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4577904Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4578227Z 
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4578729Z [32m[4;32mReady to continue?
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4579045Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4590687Z 
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4591271Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4599413Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4599957Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4600186Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4600334Z 
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4600481Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4600665Z 
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4600887Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4601249Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4601424Z 
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4601517Z If you would like to
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4601777Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4601915Z 
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4602094Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-11T05:31:54.4602384Z   $ sh ./install-nix
